/-!
# Candidate explicit Fi22 unitary coordinates

Each ambient label is assigned a six-digit base-four vector, with the first
coordinate in the least significant digit. Digits 0, 1, 2, 3 mean 0, 1, a, a+1
in `Labeling.Four`. Zero labels the distinguished singleton. Nonfixed ambient
labels are assigned zero; only the fixed-point restriction will be used.
The reverse lookup chooses the original ambient label of a normalized isotropic
vector, and otherwise returns the distinguished base point.

These are numerical data, not certificates. Their validation belongs to the
coordinate and action proofs importing this file. The discovery checks all
pairs against the literal shared ATLAS conjugate words.

Source: ATLAS F22G1-p3510B0, attributed in `AtlasCarriers/source/README.md`;
GLS3 Table 5.3t, `refs/KGroup/GLS3/Chapter5(sec3-).tex`.
-/

